diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..77ef618 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,38 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+Sign-up now collects a mobile number including its country code, sends a six-digit
+SMS code through Twilio Verify, and checks the code on the server before calling
+the existing registration service. No account is created when a code is rejected.
+
+1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`, and set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`,
+   `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID`. These are server-only
+   secrets; deployment environment variables are also supported.
+2. Configure the Twilio Verify service to use **six-digit codes**. For automatic
+   extraction, configure domain-bound SMS for the exact deployed hostname. The
+   SMS must end with a line such as `@news.example #123456`, using the actual
+   generated code. See [Twilio domain-bound SMS setup](https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/developers/tutorials/product/domain-bound-sms-otps-verify).
+3. Serve the application over HTTPS. Supported browsers can retrieve the SMS via
+   WebOTP with user permission; `autocomplete="one-time-code"` also enables
+   platform autofill. Manual typing and pasting work without WebOTP support.
+
+The endpoint fails with a service-unavailable message when credentials are absent;
+it never substitutes a simulated code. Trials may require verified recipient
+numbers. No live SMS is sent by the automated tests.
+
+Challenges are stored in the Astro session, expire after ten minutes, allow five
+code checks, and have a 30-second resend cooldown. Node's default session storage
+uses the filesystem; use a shared session driver when deploying multiple replicas.
+Enable Twilio's fraud protection and service rate limits for deployment; the local
+cooldown is per session.
+
+The existing external registration API receives `{ username, password, phone }`
+after verification. This repository cannot change that external service's access
+policy or persistence. To enforce verified phone numbers for every registration,
+its owner must restrict direct registration access and persist the verified number.
+
+Run `pnpm test` (Node 22.18+ or Node 24+) for mocked provider and registration tests,
+and `pnpm build` for a production build.
